# Applies to every image built from this repo root (currently only
# infra/docker/backend.Dockerfile). Its COPY instructions are all explicit
# (e.g. `COPY services/backend services/backend`), never `COPY . .`, but
# Docker still applies .dockerignore to those paths — without this file, a
# local pre-built services/backend/node_modules or dist (from running
# `pnpm install`/`pnpm build` on the host, e.g. for local dev/tests) gets
# copied straight into the build stage's services/backend directory,
# overwriting the node_modules that stage's own `pnpm install` just
# produced for the *target* platform. That's silently wrong output on any
# cross-architecture build (e.g. building linux/amd64 for Cloud Run from an
# arm64/Oracle dev machine, or vice versa) — excluding these forces every
# build to only ever use what RUN pnpm install produces inside the image.

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.git
.env
.env.*

# Not needed by the backend image and would otherwise bloat the build
# context sent to the Docker/Cloud Build daemon — the Dockerfile never
# COPYs these paths.
apps/mobile
docs
infra/n8n
infra/oracle-cloud
